{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgcz8UtboWs1Py5Dp1yBZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RySsdJAkbVN5nJmxZCAjnv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> docs/harness/log.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 2026-11-01: Collect the checks on uploaded files (issue #36861)\n\n**Changed**\n\n- `file_ensure_uploaded()` in `core/file_api.php` now does all checks on one uploaded file, in a fixed order: antispam, empty name, PHP upload error (any code other than `UPLOAD_ERR_OK`), name length, file type, empty `tmp_name`, readability, empty file, maximum size. A file array without an `error` key is valid (REST files have none).\n- `file_add()`, `IssueAddCommand`, `IssueFileAddCommand`, `IssueNoteAddCommand` (during validation, for each file) and `proj_doc_update.php` call it. The duplicated checks were removed from these places.\n- New `file_filter_not_selected()`: the commands remove the entries that web forms send for an empty file input (`name` empty and `UPLOAD_ERR_NO_FILE`) before they check the files.\n- `proj_doc_update.php` no longer ignores web server upload errors (before, a file with an upload error was skipped and only the title was saved).\n- `ERROR_FILE_NAME_TOO_LONG` now maps to HTTP 400 in `error_map_api_error_to_http_status()` (it gave 500).\n- Tests: `tests/Mantis/FileEnsureUploadedTest.php`, plus REST tests in `RestIssueTest` and `RestIssueNotesTest`.\n\n**Learned**\n\n- `IssueAddCommand` needs the SOAP `mci_*` helpers, so it is easier to test through the REST suite than in `tests/Mantis/`.\n- `MantisCoreBase::login()` makes assertions, so `@doesNotPerformAssertions` gives a risky test, and the full gate reports it.\n- To test `antispam_check()`, set `$g_allow_signup` in `$GLOBALS` and clear `$g_cache_config_eval['g_allow_signup']`; it is a global option and `config_set()` cannot change it.\n\n**Left**\n\n- SOAP `mci_file_add()` (`api/soap/mc_file_api.php`) writes the content itself and does 